@startuml screens
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/screens.puml
' purpose: Live StarChess Screen HUD — regions, chrome, live vs review.
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Screen HUD (apps/starchess)

package "Screen grid\n(top · board · footer)\nrows: minmax(0,auto) · auto · minmax(0,auto)\n(= apps/ui Screen)" {
  component "SidebarInset (top)\nResourceBar (live viewer)\nor ReviewTurnNav ‹ ResourceBars ›\n(review)" as TOP <<app>>
  component "BoardArea\nBoardColumn + side rail" as MID <<app>>
  component "Footer\nGasDeploy (live) · status / outcome" as BOT <<app>>
}

package "Board column" {
  component "LiveStarChessBoard\n→ AnimationStage\n→ StarChessBoard" as BOARD <<app>>
  component "DeployModal / PromotionModal" as MODALS <<app>>
}

package "Shared BoardSideRail\n(single aside + geometry + responsive hiding)" {
  component "BoardSideRail\ncontrols slot · divider · SideRailTools" as RAIL <<app>>
  component "TurnBarSidebar (live)\nTurn · Phase · queue · timer · End Turn" as LIVE <<app>>
  component "TurnBarSidebar (review)\nTurn · Phase chips only\n(DualNav → top ReviewTurnNav)" as REV <<app>>
  component "SideRailTools\nHome (+ ExitGameConfirm if live)\nreview vision · optional Flip" as TOOLS <<app>>
}

package "Dynamic band chrome\n(mobile · min-width 480px · max-height 639px)\nDYNAMIC_MOBILE_MQ — utils/breakpoints.ts + hooks/useMediaQuery.ts" {
  component "MobileBanner\natoms/MobileBanner\nBack (onBack or href) · resources · turn" as BANNER <<app>>
  component "Floating docks (fixed bottom-right)\nGasRack (live) · ReviewTurnNav ‹ › (review)\nportaled — pin to viewport, not the grid" as DOCK <<app>>
}

package "Menu modals (NeonModal atom)" {
  component "NeonModal\natoms/NeonModal" as NEON <<app>>
  component "Credits / NewGamePanel /\nExitGameConfirm (features)" as MENU <<app>>
}

package "Legacy / stories" {
  component "TurnBar (horizontal)\nturnChrome=bar only" as BAR <<async>>
}

TOP ARROW_MAIN MID
MID ARROW_MAIN BOT
TOP ARROW_OPTIONAL BANNER : dynamic band — inset chrome stands down
MID ARROW_OPTIONAL DOCK : overlays the board corner
MID ARROW_MAIN BOARD
MID ARROW_MAIN RAIL
RAIL ARROW_MAIN LIVE : live controls
RAIL ARROW_OPTIONAL REV : review controls
RAIL ARROW_MAIN TOOLS
LIVE ARROW_OPTIONAL BAR : alt chrome
BOARD ARROW_OPTIONAL MODALS
TOOLS ARROW_ERROR TOOLS : Leave Match modal
MENU ARROW_MAIN NEON

note bottom
  **Layout** matches ``apps/ui`` ``Screen`` (content-sized rows; desktop
  header ``min-height: calc(--avatar-height + 1rem)`` for captures). BoardArea = BoardColumn +
  ``BoardSideRail`` (``--sidebar-width`` only — no board-height lock).
  ``ReviewDemoScreen``, ``StarChessScreen``, and ``TutorialReviewHost`` supply
  mode-specific controls to the same rail shell.
  **Live route** ``/single``: ``turnChrome="sidebar"`` (StarChessSingleScreen);
  title ``Game vs Adjutant (Script)`` above ResourceBar; hidden when
  ``max-height: 639px`` (dynamic / short — height only, not width).
  GasDeploy floats bottom-right on the same short height (footer spacer collapses);
  idle ``Plan your turn`` status line is hidden then too.
  **Review / gameOver:** ``ReviewTurnNav`` (green ‹ ›) flanks dual ResourceBars
  in the top row; rail keeps Turn/Phase chips + Home (no stacked DualNav).
  Review detail also shows result + matchup Labels above DualNav.
  Outcome via status line (no GameOverBanner in apps/starchess).
  **Dynamic band** (``DYNAMIC_MOBILE_MQ``, e.g. Storybook Dynamic 560×420) —
  one ``MobileBanner`` strip per screen, in-flow chrome hidden:
  ``/single`` Back · fixed-width ResourceBar (12rem, ``fixedResources``:
  tracks flip to 4rem · auto · 1fr so the slack sits left of End Turn) ·
  compact TurnBar;
  ``/review/:id`` Back · dual ResourceBars (arrows move to the dock);
  ``/review`` Back · compact ``MatchHistoryFilters`` (swatches + date pager,
  no "Playing as" caption) — ``MobileBanner href`` keeps link navigation;
  ``/tutorial`` Back · compact TurnBar (live lessons; ``turnChrome="none"`` ones
  carry Back alone) and **no** ResourceBar — the coach header collapses in this
  band, and the rail / footer TurnBar are both off, so the strip is the only
  place Back and End Turn have. Replay lessons get theirs from
  ``TutorialReviewHost`` (Back · ``ReviewTurnNav`` + phase label).
  Bottom-right dock is the one floating-control slot: GasRack when live,
  ``ReviewTurnNav`` ‹ › when reviewing (same rack fill / border).
  **Tutorial** ``/tutorial/:section/:story`` (``TUTORIAL_SCRIPT`` anchors):
  CoachScreen-shaped Kerrigan header; HOME-only SideRailTools (``homeOnly``);
  no ResourceBars; fog Chess|StarChess skin toggle;
  **Fog skin demo** — each fog lesson plays the toggle itself: Chess at 1s,
  back to StarChess at 3s, so "same moves as Chess" is shown, not just claimed.
  Board hints hold until it ends (3s); non-fog lessons have no demo, so theirs
  land at once. Working the toggle by hand cancels the demo and releases the
  hints early — it never fights the player's hand.
  resolve ``combat-chain`` shows ``TurnBarSidebar`` phase chips (DualNav off);
  resolve/king footer is typewriter turn/phase nav (‹ Turn · Check · Intent · Resolve ›).
  **Guide bubble placement** (``TutorialGuideBubble``) — the line never takes a
  click meant for what it overlaps (``pointer-events`` only on its × and CTA),
  and stays in the top region beside / over Kerrigan, so the board is never
  covered. ``TutorialReviewHost`` overrides desktop to park it right of the
  board: that header has no desktop coach, only the review ‹ › it would sit on.
  desktop (≥720) docks it one rail-width right of her head; tall mobile
  (≤719 × ≥640) docks it *upward* from the chrome track floor, so it lands just
  above rank 8 — close enough to the board to read as being about it — and grows
  toward Kerrigan rather than over the board. The track floor is the board's top
  edge only because ``BaseScreen`` / ``TutorialReviewHost`` ``.headerSlot`` fills
  the track on mobile (chrome still packs to its top); an auto bottom margin left
  the line stranded an avatar's height above the board.
  Both cap at ``--avatar-height`` — the band they grow into — and scroll past
  that. Short / dynamic mobile alone keeps the centred float over ranks 7–8:
  neither axis has the room to dodge the board there.
  **Chess skin** (``cburnett``) — chosen only by ``TutorialScreen`` (fog stage),
  read only by presentation glyph switches: ``RookGlyph`` flattens tank/siege,
  ``kingDamageOverlay`` flattens a burning Command Center (HP 1–2) to the classic
  King. Never a rules concept — asserted in ``__tests__/bundle/bundleBoundary``.
  Fire cues pass the same fog gate as every other cue layer, so an unseen
  burning CC never marks its square (``__tests__/fog/kingDamageFog``).
  **Tutorial-only labels** (``TutorialHudLabels``) — names the deploy /
  promotion tiles (``specialCopyFor``) and the three ResourceBar strips.
  Anchors are found by test id and measured into a portal, so ``DeployModal`` /
  ``PromotionModal`` / ``ResourceBar`` carry no tutorial branch.
  **Full-match exception:** final lesson ``king-attack-3`` (``fullMatchHud``)
  renders the ``/single``-style top pane — Home + matchTitle + ResourceBar +
  status line — with no coach header / mobile hero; guide bubble docks below
  the pane (``hudGuideSlot``). Status line is gated ``!tutorial || fullMatchHud``
  (hidden for the other tutorials).
  **Animation clock:** ``_spec/apps/starchess/animation-pipeline.md``.
end note
@enduml
